{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"fetch","tool":"fetch","arguments":{"max_length":16000,"raw":false,"start_index":0,"url":"https://ukraine.ohchr.org/en/reports/detention"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contents of https://ukraine.ohchr.org/en/reports/detention:\nHuman rights for everyone everywhere.\n\n \n\n* ABOUT US\n  + [Our work](/en/aboutus/ourwork)\n  + [Head of Mission](/en/aboutus/headofmission)\n  + [Offices](/en/aboutus/offices)\n  + [Job opportunities](/en/aboutus/jobopportunities)\n  + [FAQ](/en/aboutus/faq)\n* OUR REPORTS\n  + [Periodic reports on the human rights situation in Ukraine](/en/reports/periodic-reports-on-the-human-rights-situation-in-ukraine)\n  + [Thematic human rights reports](/en/reports/thematic-human-rights-reports)\n    - [Crimea and other occupied territory](/en/reports/crimea-and-occupied-territory)\n    - [Detention and prisoners of war](/en/reports/detention)\n    - [Civic space](/en/reports/civic-space)\n    - [Conflict-related sexual violence](/en/reports/crsv)\n  + [Protection of civilians](/en/reports/protection-of-civilians)\n  + [Reports of the Secretary-General](/en/reports/reports-of-the-secretary-general)\n    - [Crimea and other occupied territory](/en/reports/crimea-and-occupied-territory-secretary-general)\n    - [Conflict-related sexual violence](/en/reports/conflict-related-sexual-violence)\n    - [Children and armed conflict](/en/reports/children-and-armed-conflict)\n    - [Protection of civilians](/en/reports/protection-of-civilians-secretary-general)\n  + [Other publications](/en/reports/other-publications)\n  + [All reports](/en/reports)\n* RESOURCES\n  + [Key Human Rights documents](/en/key-human-rights-documents)\n* MEDIA CENTER\n  + [Latest news](/en/mediacenter/latestnews)\n  + [Events](/en/mediacenter/events)\n  + [Featured Stories](/en/gallery)\n  + [Media contacts](/en/mediacenter/mediacontacts)\n\n[![Home](/sites/default/files/logonew_0.png)](/en)\n\n* ABOUT US\n  + [Our work](/en/aboutus/ourwork)\n  + [Head of Mission](/en/aboutus/headofmission)\n  + [Offices](/en/aboutus/offices)\n  + [Job opportunities](/en/aboutus/jobopportunities)\n  + [FAQ](/en/aboutus/faq)\n* OUR REPORTS\n  + [Periodic reports on the human rights situation in Ukraine](/en/reports/periodic-reports-on-the-human-rights-situation-in-ukraine)\n  + [Thematic human rights reports](/en/reports/thematic-human-rights-reports)\n    - [Crimea and other occupied territory](/en/reports/crimea-and-occupied-territory)\n    - [Detention and prisoners of war](/en/reports/detention)\n    - [Civic space](/en/reports/civic-space)\n    - [Conflict-related sexual violence](/en/reports/crsv)\n  + [Protection of civilians](/en/reports/protection-of-civilians)\n  + [Reports of the Secretary-General](/en/reports/reports-of-the-secretary-general)\n    - [Crimea and other occupied territory](/en/reports/crimea-and-occupied-territory-secretary-general)\n    - [Conflict-related sexual violence](/en/reports/conflict-related-sexual-violence)\n    - [Children and armed conflict](/en/reports/children-and-armed-conflict)\n    - [Protection of civilians](/en/reports/protection-of-civilians-secretary-general)\n  + [Other publications](/en/reports/other-publications)\n  + [All reports](/en/reports)\n* RESOURCES\n  + [Key Human Rights documents](/en/key-human-rights-documents)\n* MEDIA CENTER\n  + [Latest news](/en/mediacenter/latestnews)\n  + [Events](/en/mediacenter/events)\n  + [Featured Stories](/en/gallery)\n  + [Media contacts](/en/mediacenter/mediacontacts)\n\n  \n\nFilter\n\n* ![](/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/2025-09/ENG%20detention%20cover%C2%A0%E2%80%94%20%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BF%D0%B8%D1%8F.png.webp?itok=C6YxJfcN)\n\n  23 September 2025\n\n  Large-scale deprivation of liberty, affecting both of civilians and military personnel, remains a stark reality in the ongoing armed attack of the Russian Federation against Ukraine. Building on previous OHCHR findings, this report describes the treatment of civilians deprived of their liberty for reasons related to the armed conflict since 2022.\n* ![](/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/2023-09/1_1.png.webp?itok=BXZ4uQKf)\n\n  27 June 2023\n\n  This report by the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights (OHCHR) examines the detention of civilians in the context of the armed attack by the Russian Federation against Ukraine. The report covers the period from 24 February 2022 to 23 May 2023 and is based on the findings of the United Nations Human Rights Monitoring Mission in Ukraine (HRMMU).\n* ![](/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/2023-05/POW%20cover%20ENG.png.webp?itok=fX3NyCjA)\n\n  24 March 2023\n\n  This report by the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights (OHCHR) focuses on the treatment of prisoners of war (POWs) by the parties to the international armed conflict since the large- scale armed attack by the Russian Federation against Ukraine commencing on 24 February 2022. The report covers the period from 24 February 2022 to 23 February 2023 and is based on the findings of the Human Rights Monitoring Mission in Ukraine.\n* ![](/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/2024-01/%D0%97%D0%BD%D1%96%D0%BC%D0%BE%D0%BA%20%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B0%202024-01-23%20%D0%BE%2017.15.49_0.png.webp?itok=mr3DwVqz)\n\n  2 July 2021\n\n  This thematic report by the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights (OHCHR) examines the scale of detention in the context of the armed conflict in eastern Ukraine by Government actors and armed groups and other actors in territory controlled by the self-proclaimed ‘Donetsk people’s republic’ and the self-proclaimed ‘Luhansk people’s republic’ from 14 April 2014 to 30 April 2021.\n\n© UN Human Rights Monitoring Mission in Ukraine"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
